Subject: [PATCH] wifi_ctrl: publish association delta when a client returns

A client steered to another EasyMesh agent can disappear from the kernel
station table without sending a disassociation frame to its old AP.  OneWifi
therefore retains that AP's associated_devices_map entry.  If the client is
later steered back, assoc_dev_event() finds the old entry and does nothing: the
radio completes reassociation and the four-way handshake, but no associated
clients delta is published to the EasyMesh translator.  The controller and
WebUI remain attributed to the previous AP indefinitely.

Runtime reproduction with five agents and ten hwsim clients:

  AP-A -> AP-B: radio, controller DB, and API all update
  AP-B -> AP-A: radio reaches AP-A; controller DB and API remain on AP-B

The AP-A logs show the second authentication, reassociation, EAPOL M1..M4, and
monitor_connect, but omit assoc_dev_event's "Device ... associated" line.  Its
old map entry is the only condition that distinguishes the failed return.

Treat every connect indication as an association delta.  For an existing map
entry refresh the stored data, mark it connected, add/update the diff map, and
set the existing webconfig pending bit.  Counts and new-client notifications
remain unchanged.  This is idempotent for duplicate connect indications and
lets the controller's single-association handling replace the former owner.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 source/core/wifi_ctrl_queue_handlers.c | 22 +++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/source/core/wifi_ctrl_queue_handlers.c b/source/core/wifi_ctrl_queue_handlers.c
index 4afb906..888c0bc 100644
--- a/source/core/wifi_ctrl_queue_handlers.c
+++ b/source/core/wifi_ctrl_queue_handlers.c
@@ -2512,2 +2512,22 @@ static void assoc_dev_event(assoc_dev_data_t *assoc_data)
         }
-    }
+    } else {
+        /* A roam does not guarantee that the old AP receives a disassociation
+         * frame.  Its map can therefore still contain this client when the
+         * client later returns.  A connect indication is authoritative: refresh
+         * the entry and publish an associated delta even when the key exists. */
+        memcpy(tmp_assoc_dev_data, assoc_data, sizeof(assoc_dev_data_t));
+        tmp_assoc_dev_data->client_state = client_state_connected;
+        if (add_client_diff_assoclist(&rdk_vap_info->associated_devices_diff_map,
+                mac_str, tmp_assoc_dev_data) == RETURN_ERR) {
+            pthread_mutex_unlock(rdk_vap_info->associated_devices_lock);
+            wifi_util_error_print(WIFI_CTRL,
+                "%s:%d Failed to refresh diff assoclist for vap %d mac_str : %s\n",
+                __func__, __LINE__, rdk_vap_info->vap_index, mac_str);
+            return;
+        }
+        p_wifi_mgr->ctrl.webconfig_state |=
+            ctrl_webconfig_state_associated_clients_cfg_rsp_pending;
+        wifi_util_info_print(WIFI_CTRL,
+            "%s:%d Device %s re-associated with vapindex %d; publishing refreshed delta\n",
+            __func__, __LINE__, mac_str, rdk_vap_info->vap_index);
+    }
